 "standard-of-the-fell-warrior": "Single use. In the Remaining Moves sub-phase, just before it moves, the unit carrying this standard may redress its ranks for free; it then moves normally but may not turn or quick turn. The line reforms in silence, as if of one mind.",
 "wizarding-hat": "The wearer becomes a Level 1 Wizard knowing one random spell from a Lore of Magic you pick, but suffers from Stupidity, for the spirit inside the hat mutters endlessly. Its first owner never quite left it.",
 "arch-lightning-rod": "Single use. In the Command sub-phase of their own turn, if not in melee, the bearer may take a Resolve test on their own unmodified Resolve. If passed, enemy units may not use the Fly (X) special rule until the Start of Turn sub-phase of your next turn. The sky itself turns hostile to wings.",
 "flying-carpet": "Regular or heavy infantry only. The bearer may not join a unit, but has both Swiftstride and Fly (8). Bought far beyond the Sundered Lands, and worth every coin.",
