 "potion-of-fervour": "Single use. The bearer may drink it in the Command sub-phase of their own turn; until the end of that turn they gain +D3 Strikes (maximum 10). A model may drink only one potion of any kind each Command phase. For a few heartbeats, the drinker fights like a saint.",
 "potion-of-strength": "Single use. The bearer may drink it in the Command sub-phase of their own turn; until the end of that turn they gain +D3 Might (maximum 10). Extremely common. Mostly turnip, partly spell.",
 "ring-of-doom": "Holds Ruinbolt, a Lore of Dark Magic spell, as a Bound spell with Power Level 2. Each time it is cast successfully, your opponent rolls a D6; on 4+ the bearer loses 1 Resilience (to no lower than 1). The rot spreads up the finger with every use.",
 "potion-of-toughness": "Single use. The bearer may drink it in the Command sub-phase of their own turn; until the end of that turn they gain +D3 Resilience (maximum 10). Extremely common. The drinker's skin goes hard as old leather.",
 "becalming-orb": "Single use. The bearer may cast this Bound spell at Power Level 1: a Hex with casting value 8+ that targets the caster (range Self). Any enemy Wizard within 15\" of the caster adds 2 to the casting value of each spell they attempt, lasting until the Start of Turn sub-phase of your next turn. The crystal drinks the Weave from the air around it.",
 "unmade-blooded-steed": "Cavalry only. The bearer's mount gains +1 Movement, +1 Might and +1 Strikes (maximum 10) but also the Impetuous special rule. Somewhere in its bloodline, something Unmade was let into the stable.",
 "elixir-of-power": "Single use. The bearer may drink it in the Command sub-phase of their own turn; until the Start of Turn sub-phase of their next turn they gain +1 Might, +1 Strikes and +1 Reflexes (maximum 10). When it wears off they lose 1 Hit Point, which no Regeneration save can prevent. The price of greatness, paid in the morning.",
 "potion-of-speed": "Single use. The bearer may drink it in the Command sub-phase of their own turn; until the end of that turn they gain +D3 Reflexes (maximum 10). Extremely common. It tastes of burnt copper.",
 "potion-of-foolhardiness": "Single use. The bearer may drink it in the Command sub-phase of their own turn and has the Immune To Psychology special rule until the end of that turn. Extremely common. Suspiciously like plain spirits.",
